133
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:23,200
The person who's explaining all of these interesting things is saying that, well, in any case, to take better advantage of the daylight available, we compensate by moving our clocks forward one hour.

134
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:27,040
This is an important phrase you could say to take better advantage of or to take advantage of.

135
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:28,300
Let's talk about this.

136
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,760
To take advantage of something.

137
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:33,640
So to take advantage of something is to use it efficiently, right?

138
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,330
Or to take better advantage.

139
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:49,200
So for example, if you drive to work every day and your neighbor drives to work every day and you work at the same place, you could take better advantage of your car and the cost by sharing the same car to work.

140
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:49,740
Exactly.

141
00:07:50,320 --> 00:08:00,040
Or when people started to use computers, you could say, well, they were taking better advantage of their time by speeding things up, by making things faster with the computers.

142
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:01,040
Right.

143
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:05,880
Or many mothers say, take better advantage of your time and read something instead of playing those video games.

144
00:08:06,320 --> 00:08:06,560
Exactly.

145
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:12,920
So it means, like you said, to be more efficient, to do useful or important things.

146
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:13,160
That's right.

147
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:20,600
And now when we talked about what daylight savings time means or GMT, what that stands for.

148
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:21,360
This is an interesting phrase.

149
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,400
It stands for.

150
00:08:23,400 --> 00:08:25,290
Well, think about it as a picture.

151
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:31,720
So if something stands for something else, that means the original thing, it's not there anymore.

152
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:38,810
And so in words and phrases like GMT, GMT doesn't mean anything by itself.

153
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:42,040
But the G stands for something, the M stands for something.

154
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:42,550
It's an acronym.

155
00:08:43,040 --> 00:08:44,040
Okay.

156
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:49,200
So this is an acronym that stands for, that represents three big long words.

157
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,200
Okay.

158
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,200
Greenwich, meantime.

159
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:52,200
Right.

160
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:59,800
So we use this a lot when we are defining words or when we are defining an acronym like GMT stands for Greenwich, meantime.

161
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:04,300
Or for example, USA stands for United States of America.

162
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:07,760
Or we can even say someone's name stands for something.

163
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:11,520
So Marco, what is the M in your last name stand for?

